          ],
          "reasons": [
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "t": "text",
                  "v": "False. The coin has no memory: each flip is independent, so P(tails) is still ½. Over many flips the proportion settles near ½ because later flips swamp early runs, not because they balance them out.",
                },
              ],
              "id": "RA",
            },
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "t": "text",
                  "v": "True. Five heads in a row is impossible for a fair coin.",
